export const html = "<h1 id=\"chapter-6--meme-studio\">Chapter 6 · Meme Studio</h1>\n<blockquote>\n<p>How you actually turn a fact into a meme — with your own photo as its\nbackground — and what's true underneath.</p>\n<p>Deep spec: <a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/meme-and-video-studio.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\"><code>meme-and-video-studio.md</code></a>.\nRelated: <a href=\"/admin/help/5-visual-pipeline\" data-help-internal=\"/admin/help/5-visual-pipeline\"><code>5-visual-pipeline.md</code></a> (the image\nmachinery moderation uses), <a href=\"/admin/help/10-payments-and-membership\" data-help-internal=\"/admin/help/10-payments-and-membership\"><code>10-payments-and-membership.md</code></a>\n(what <a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#legendary\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">Legendary</a> unlocks).</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2 id=\"what-it-does\">What it does</h2>\n<p>Once you've found a fact you want to make into a meme, the <a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#studio\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">studio</a> is where\nyou actually build it. You can build a meme from your own photo or from a\nstock image. Whichever\n<a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#background\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">background</a> you choose, the studio composes it with the fact's text and\nsaves it as your meme.</p>\n<h2 id=\"how-it-works\">How it works</h2>\n<h3 id=\"building-a-background\">Building a background</h3>\n<p>Upload a photo, or pick a <a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#stock-image\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">stock image</a>.\nThis is available to anyone signed in — no paid plan required. The built-in\ngradient backgrounds were deleted before launch (the record is in\n<a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/retired/README.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\"><code>docs/retired/</code></a>).</p>\n<p>There are no AI-generated memes and no video memes. Both were deleted before\nlaunch, to be rebuilt later on stronger models: the AI image of you in the\nfact's scene (PuLID) and video\n(<a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/decisions.md#2026-10-05--launch-scope-video-deferred-the-share-loop-and-open-graph-previews-launch-critical-and-the-rest-of-the-feature-walk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">decisions</a>; the record is in\n<a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/retired/README.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\"><code>docs/retired/</code></a>).</p>\n<p>You build memes in one of two places. On a fact's page, the builder opens\nstraight onto the image you'll make. On a shared meme's page, \"make this about me\" opens a\nsingle-screen builder that remakes that meme for you. An older studio that used to\nsit behind the fact page was deleted before launch\n(<a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/decisions.md#2026-10-22--the-legacy-meme-studio-is-deleted-the-user-generate-route-survives-photo-only-until-pulid-goes\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">decisions</a>).</p>\n<h3 id=\"what-actually-gets-saved\">What actually gets saved</h3>\n<p>A meme you build from your own photo or a stock image isn't\nstored as a finished picture — it's saved as a <strong><a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#recipe\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">recipe</a></strong>: which\nbackground you chose and what text goes with it. The actual image is\ncomposed fresh every time someone views it, not generated once and stored.\nLike any meme, it's public unless you turn the privacy option on yourself.</p>\n<h3 id=\"where-your-media-lives\">Where your media lives</h3>\n<p>A photo you uploaded is a real file, stored the same way any other user\ncontent on Overhype.me is stored. A meme built from a stock photo stores no\nimage of its own at all, just the recipe pointing back at the\nalready-existing stock photo.</p>\n<h2 id=\"why-it-works-this-way\">Why it works this way</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Saving a recipe instead of a picture keeps a meme current.</strong> If Overhype.me improves how memes are composed — better text\nplacement, a rendering fix — a recipe-based meme picks that improvement\nup automatically the next time anyone views it, instead of being frozen\nat whatever quality existed the moment it was made.</li>\n<li><strong>Making a meme is free for everyone signed in.</strong> Building from your own\nphoto or a stock background costs Overhype.me nothing extra per\nmeme. What Legendary adds here is keeping a meme private\n(<a href=\"/admin/help/10-payments-and-membership\" data-help-internal=\"/admin/help/10-payments-and-membership\">chapter 10</a>).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"boundaries--known-limitations\">Boundaries &#x26; known limitations</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Uploading your own photo to build a meme isn't currently paywalled</strong>,\neven though the product has machinery elsewhere that suggests it might\nonce have been intended to be. <strong>Needs David confirmation</strong> on whether\nthat's the intended, permanent behavior.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"going-deeper\">Going deeper</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Spec: <a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/meme-and-video-studio.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\"><code>meme-and-video-studio.md</code></a>\n— the exact routes, the recipe/<code>imageSource</code> shape, tier-gate specifics,\nand the storage layout.</li>\n<li>Related: <a href=\"/admin/help/5-visual-pipeline\" data-help-internal=\"/admin/help/5-visual-pipeline\"><code>5-visual-pipeline.md</code></a> (the image\nmachinery moderation uses), <a href=\"/admin/help/10-payments-and-membership\" data-help-internal=\"/admin/help/10-payments-and-membership\"><code>10-payments-and-membership.md</code></a>\n(what Legendary unlocks generally).</li>\n<li>Rationale: the studio/media entries in <a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/decisions.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\"><code>decisions.md</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Next:</strong> chapter 7 — <a href=\"/admin/help/7-public-site-and-sharing\" data-help-internal=\"/admin/help/7-public-site-and-sharing\"><code>7-public-site-and-sharing.md</code></a>,\nhome, search, <a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#hashtags\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">hashtags</a>, leaderboard,\nprofiles, OG cards, and sharing — the surfaces\nthe loop closes through.</p>\n<p><em>Verified against <code>e9669d2</code> (2026-08-09) · claim inventory in PR #371.</em></p>";
